Package: corrkit
Title: Correlation Analyses with Annotated Heatmaps and Tables
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Clément", "Poupelin", email = "clementjc.poupelin@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A thin layer over validated correlation engines (stats::cor.test(),
    ppcor::pcor.test(), psych::corr.test(), correlation::correlation()) that adds
    one way of working: an explicit multiple-testing family, a dedicated reading
    of binary (0/1) variables, and publication-ready outputs (ggplot2 heatmaps and
    scatter plots, gt tables) whose subtitles, captions and source notes state the
    method, the engine, the formulas, the adjustment and how to read the result.
    Notation follows Makowski, Ben-Shachar, Patil and Lüdecke (2020)
    <doi:10.21105/joss.02306>.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
